                <pb facs="0272" n="184" xml:id="pg184"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Conger</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Our position, payment indemnity in silver, is not attempted new interpretation of
                    terms protocol; but the United States Government has always understood this to
                    be meaning of agreement. The President reserves full liberty of action whatever
                    may be decision reached.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
